DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Individual Fellowship 2027 (up to 
 USD 35\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship supports sel
 f-directed exploration and cultural exchange experiences in a new or less 
 familiar environment\, fostering exchange between the United States and As
 ia and within Asia. SUPPORT: up to USD 35\,000 for a 1-to-6-month program 
 (minimum 30 days\; two or more months preferred)\; single or joint applica
 tions with up to 3 participants.\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council\n
 Location: Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or wit
 hin Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (
 including the US).\nAward: Up to USD 35\,000 for self-directed exploration
  and cultural exchange of 1 to 6 months. Single or joint applications (up 
 to 3 participants). No application fee.\nDuration: 1 to 6 months (minimum 
 30 days\; 2 or more months preferred)\, with grant activities between 1 Au
 gust 2027 and 31 December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil.o
 rg/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Self-directed cultural exchange between the US and Asia\, or withi
 n Asia. For citizens and permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries (in
 cluding the US).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eulsukdo-busan-land-ecological-art-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Busan Metropolitan City: Open Call for Land / Ecological 
 Art on Eulsukdo
DESCRIPTION:Busan Metropolitan City invites individuals and teams from arou
 nd the world to propose a site-responsive work of land and ecological art 
 for Eulsukdo\, an estuarine island at the mouth of the Nakdong River\, Sou
 th Korea's longest river.\n\nOrganisation: Busan Metropolitan City\, Urban
  Parks Division\nLocation: Eulsukdo\, Busan\, South Korea (site at 1142-8 
 Hadan-dong\, Saha-gu). Open to individuals and teams worldwide\; the commi
 ssioned work is realised on site.\nAward: One proposal selected. Artwork s
 upport KRW 380\,000\,000 (approx. EUR 235\,000) plus artist fee KRW 20\,00
 0\,000 (approx. EUR 12\,500). No entry fee indicated.\nDuration: Single co
 mmission\; provisional opening May to June 2027.\n\nMore: https://eulsukdo
 -ecoart.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eulsukdo-ecoart.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
LOCATION:Eulsukdo\, Busan\, South Korea (site at 1142-8 Hadan-dong\, Saha-g
 u). Open to individuals and teams worldwide\; the commissioned work is rea
 lised on site.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acc-organization-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council Organization Grant 2027 (up to USD
  50\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Organization Grant funds arts and 
 culture organisations to send participants on cultural exchange between th
 e US and Asia or within Asia. SUPPORT: up to USD 50\,000.\n\nOrganisation:
  Asian Cultural Council\nLocation: Cultural exchange travel between the US
  and Asia\, or within Asia. For nonprofit\, government-affiliated or acade
 mic organisations registered in ACC-eligible locations.\nAward: Up to USD 
 50\,000 per organisation for exchange travel by its participants. No appli
 cation fee.\nDuration: 1 to 6 months of travel (at least 30 consecutive da
 ys in the US\, or 30 cumulative days in Asia)\, with activities between 1 
 August 2027 and 31 December 2028\n\nMore: https://www.asianculturalcouncil
 .org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cultural exchange travel between the US and Asia\, or within Asia.
  For nonprofit\, government-affiliated or academic organisations registere
 d in ACC-eligible locations.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151758Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 .\n\nOrganisation: Daiwa Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individu
 als\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running
  projects that connect the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (ty
 pical awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsis
 tence up to GBP 100 per person per day. A contribution\, not full funding.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\; activity can start from late
  May or early June 2027.\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-pr
 izes/daiwa-foundation-small-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
